  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Projectmanagement of the Young Expert Programme Energy - Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of 2020, the Young Expert Program (YEP) has been expanded to include YEP Energy. YEP started in 2013 with YEP Water - the Netherlands Water Partnership (NWP) was established as the program office at that time. With the expansion to YEP Agrofood, the Food Business Knowledge Platform (FBKP) was recruited as a networking partner for this sector. With the expansion with YEP Energy, the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO), which already implements several programs for BZ (MFA) in the field of (access to) renewable energy, takes on the role of project manager and network partner for YEP Energy. In this capacity, RVO supports the NWP/YEP Program Office in the implementation of the YEP program. The activity concerns purely the deployment of RVO on behalf of YEP Energy. Other costs for the implementation of YEP Energy are part of the agreement with the NWP/YEP Program Office. The following activities will be performed by RFO&apos;s YEP Energy project manager: - Identifying organizations that could make use of YEP Energy - Engaging these organizations - Identifying organizations that could nominate young experts for YEP Energy and involving them in the program - Presentation during YEP information sessions and promotion of YEP Energy during energy events - Reviewing proposals and CVs (incl. speed dates with candidates) - Preparation and participation of Steering Committee - Providing input to YEP Annual Plan - Preparation of Renewable Energy Masterclass</narrative>
  </description>
